# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Import the packages and define two helpers: one that trains a random forest, and one that computes the metrics used throughout the tutorial.\n"
msgstr "Import pakej dan takrifkan dua fungsi pembantu: satu untuk melatih random forest, dan satu lagi untuk mengira metrik yang digunakan sepanjang tutorial ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure IBM Quantum credentials {#configure-ibm-quantum-credentials}"
msgstr "Konfigurasikan kelayakan IBM Quantum {#configure-ibm-quantum-credentials}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authenticate with your [IBM Quantum Platform API key](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/), load the Rimay function, and select the least busy quantum processor available to your instance.\n"
msgstr "Sahkan identiti dengan [kunci API IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/) anda, muatkan fungsi Rimay, dan pilih pemproses kuantum paling kurang sibuk yang tersedia untuk instance anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay maps every numerical input feature onto one qubit, so the first step is to turn the raw table into numerical features.\n"
msgstr "Rimay memetakan setiap ciri input berangka kepada satu qubit, jadi langkah pertama ialah menukar jadual mentah kepada ciri berangka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the dataset {#load-the-dataset}"
msgstr "Muatkan set data {#load-the-dataset}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the German credit dataset directly from OpenML. The `class` column holds the label: `good` for applicants who repaid their credit and `bad` for those who did not.\n"
msgstr "Muatkan set data kredit Jerman terus daripada OpenML. Lajur `class` mengandungi label: `good` untuk pemohon yang membayar balik kredit mereka dan `bad` untuk yang tidak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encode the features {#encode-the-features}"
msgstr "Kodkan ciri {#encode-the-features}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convert the label to a binary value, and one-hot encode the 13 categorical columns. The code drops the first category of each column to avoid redundant features, which results in 48 numerical features.\n"
msgstr "Tukarkan label kepada nilai binari, dan kodkan one-hot 13 lajur kategori. Kod ini membuang kategori pertama bagi setiap lajur untuk mengelakkan ciri berlebihan, yang menghasilkan 48 ciri berangka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split into training and test sets {#split-into-training-and-test-sets}"
msgstr "Pisahkan kepada set latihan dan set ujian {#split-into-training-and-test-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hold back 20% of the applicants as a test set. A stratified split keeps the share of good and bad credits equal in both sets.\n"
msgstr "Asingkan 20% pemohon sebagai set ujian. Pemisahan berstrata mengekalkan perkadaran kredit baik dan buruk yang sama dalam kedua-dua set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Establish a classical baseline {#establish-a-classical-baseline}"
msgstr "Tetapkan garis dasar klasik {#establish-a-classical-baseline}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train a random forest on the classical features. In Step 4, you compare the quantum-transformed features against its metrics.\n"
msgstr "Latih random forest pada ciri klasik. Dalam Langkah 4, anda membandingkan ciri yang diubah secara kuantum dengan metriknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the data to Rimay {#upload-the-data-to-rimay}"
msgstr "Muat naik data ke Rimay {#upload-the-data-to-rimay}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay reads its inputs from CSV files that you upload to the function. The features and the labels go into separate files. You also upload the test set, so that Rimay maps it with the same mapping it fits on the training set.\n"
msgstr "Rimay membaca inputnya daripada fail CSV yang anda muat naik ke fungsi tersebut. Ciri dan label disimpan dalam fail berasingan. Anda juga memuat naik set ujian, supaya Rimay memetakannya dengan pemetaan yang sama yang dipadankan pada set latihan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan pada perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay builds and transpiles the circuits for the processor you select, so there is no circuit to optimize by hand. Specify the number of shots per circuit, within the following constraints:\n"
msgstr "Rimay membina dan men-transpile litar untuk pemproses yang anda pilih, jadi tiada litar yang perlu dioptimumkan secara manual. Nyatakan bilangan shot bagi setiap litar, dalam kekangan berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every feature needs one qubit, so the processor must have at least as many qubits as the dataset has features.\n"
msgstr "Setiap ciri memerlukan satu qubit, jadi pemproses mesti mempunyai sekurang-kurangnya sebanyak qubit seperti bilangan ciri dalam set data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay runs one circuit per row, training and test rows together. A single job can request at most 10 million executions, so the number of rows times `shots` must stay within that budget.\n"
msgstr "Rimay menjalankan satu litar bagi setiap baris, baris latihan dan ujian bersama-sama. Satu job boleh meminta paling banyak 10 juta pelaksanaan, jadi bilangan baris darab `shots` mesti kekal dalam bajet tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check both limits before you submit the job.\n"
msgstr "Semak kedua-dua had sebelum anda menghantar job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"A job must also finish within 24 hours, including the time its circuits wait in the queue, or it is stopped without a result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Sesuatu job juga mesti selesai dalam masa 24 jam, termasuk masa litarnya menunggu dalam baris gilir, jika tidak ia dihentikan tanpa hasil.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the function size {#calculate-the-function-size}"
msgstr "Kira saiz fungsi {#calculate-the-function-size}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every job runs at a function size, `S`, `M`, or `L`, which selects the compute resources it runs on. For Rimay, the size depends on the number of rows that a job maps, training and test rows together. If you request a size that is too small, the job fails with error `4600`. For the sizes and their limits, see [Function sizes](/guides/kipu-rimay#function-sizes) in the Rimay guide.\n"
msgstr "Setiap job dijalankan pada saiz fungsi, `S`, `M`, atau `L`, yang memilih sumber pengkomputeran yang digunakannya. Bagi Rimay, saiz bergantung pada bilangan baris yang dipetakan oleh sesuatu job, baris latihan dan ujian bersama-sama. Jika anda meminta saiz yang terlalu kecil, job gagal dengan ralat `4600`. Untuk saiz dan had masing-masing, lihat [Function sizes](/guides/kipu-rimay#function-sizes) dalam panduan Rimay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following cell defines the size calculator. It runs on your machine, reads only the data that you pass to it, and submits nothing.\n"
msgstr "Sel berikut mentakrifkan pengira saiz. Ia berjalan pada mesin anda, hanya membaca data yang anda berikan kepadanya, dan tidak menghantar apa-apa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the data sets in the same order as the files in `input_file`, together with the mode of the run:\n"
msgstr "Hantar set data mengikut susunan yang sama seperti fail dalam `input_file`, bersama-sama dengan mod larian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run Rimay in `fit-transform` mode. It fits a quantum feature mapping on `x_train.csv` and `y_train.csv`, and maps both the training and the test sets with it. The order of the files in `input_file` matters. List the training features, the training labels, and then the optional test features. Pass the size that you calculated as `function_size`.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan Rimay dalam mod `fit-transform`. Ia memadankan pemetaan ciri kuantum pada `x_train.csv` dan `y_train.csv`, dan memetakan kedua-dua set latihan dan ujian dengannya. Susunan fail dalam `input_file` adalah penting. Senaraikan ciri latihan, label latihan, dan kemudian ciri ujian pilihan. Hantar saiz yang anda kira sebagai `function_size`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monitor the job {#monitor-the-job}"
msgstr "Pantau job {#monitor-the-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status of the job while it runs. `job.result()` blocks until the job has finished.\n"
msgstr "Semak status job semasa ia berjalan. `job.result()` menyekat sehingga job selesai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result holds a `mapping_id`, which identifies the mapping that this run fitted. You do not need it in this tutorial, because the test set was mapped in the same run. Record this ID if you want to map new rows later with `mode=\"transform\"`. It is the only way to access the fitted mapping, and without it, you must fit and pay for a new one. The mapping is built for the qubit layout of this processor, so a later `transform` run must pass the same `backend_name`.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya mengandungi `mapping_id`, yang mengenal pasti pemetaan yang dipadankan oleh larian ini. Anda tidak memerlukannya dalam tutorial ini, kerana set ujian telah dipetakan dalam larian yang sama. Rekodkan ID ini jika anda ingin memetakan baris baharu kemudian dengan `mode=\"transform\"`. Ini satu-satunya cara untuk mengakses pemetaan yang telah dipadankan, dan tanpanya, anda perlu memadankan dan membayar untuk pemetaan baharu. Pemetaan dibina untuk susun atur qubit pemproses ini, jadi larian `transform` kemudian mesti menghantar `backend_name` yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return the result in the desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-the-result-in-the-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan pulangkan hasil dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-the-result-in-the-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download the quantum-transformed features {#download-the-quantum-transformed-features}"
msgstr "Muat turun ciri yang diubah secara kuantum {#download-the-quantum-transformed-features}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download the files that the job wrote, by using the names in `output_files`. Each name starts with the job ID, so the files of this run stay available after later runs. Pass `target_name` so that each file is saved under its own name.\n"
msgstr "Muat turun fail yang ditulis oleh job, dengan menggunakan nama dalam `output_files`. Setiap nama bermula dengan ID job, jadi fail bagi larian ini kekal tersedia selepas larian seterusnya. Hantar `target_name` supaya setiap fail disimpan di bawah namanya sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train on the quantum-transformed features {#train-on-the-quantum-transformed-features}"
msgstr "Latih pada ciri yang diubah secara kuantum {#train-on-the-quantum-transformed-features}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train a random forest on the quantum-transformed features alone.\n"
msgstr "Latih random forest pada ciri yang diubah secara kuantum sahaja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train on classical and quantum features combined {#train-on-classical-and-quantum-features-combined}"
msgstr "Latih pada ciri klasik dan kuantum yang digabungkan {#train-on-classical-and-quantum-features-combined}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stack the original and the quantum-transformed features, and train the same model on the combination.\n"
msgstr "Susun ciri asal dan ciri yang diubah secara kuantum, dan latih model yang sama pada gabungan tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the results {#compare-the-results}"
msgstr "Bandingkan hasil {#compare-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the three models on the test set.\n"
msgstr "Bandingkan ketiga-tiga model pada set ujian.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/classify-credit-risk-with-rimay-quantum-feature-extraction/extracted-outputs/321e240bb0e14c12-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/classify-credit-risk-with-rimay-quantum-feature-extraction/extracted-outputs/321e240bb0e14c12-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The AUC measures how well a model ranks good above bad credits, independent of a decision threshold, which makes it the most informative metric on this imbalanced dataset (70% good credits). In Kipu Quantum's benchmarks, the quantum-transformed features on their own reached an AUC similar to the classical baseline, and the hybrid model, which combines both, reached the highest AUC and F1 score. The quantum-transformed features therefore add information that the classical features do not provide on their own.\n"
msgstr "AUC mengukur sejauh mana baik sesebuah model meletakkan kredit baik di atas kredit buruk, tanpa bergantung pada ambang keputusan, yang menjadikannya metrik paling bermaklumat pada set data tidak seimbang ini (70% kredit baik). Dalam penanda aras Kipu Quantum, ciri yang diubah secara kuantum sahaja mencapai AUC yang serupa dengan garis dasar klasik, dan model hibrid, yang menggabungkan kedua-duanya, mencapai AUC dan skor F1 tertinggi. Oleh itu, ciri yang diubah secara kuantum menambah maklumat yang tidak disediakan oleh ciri klasik sahaja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clean up (optional) {#clean-up-optional}"
msgstr "Pembersihan (pilihan) {#clean-up-optional}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A fitted mapping stays available until you delete it. If you do not want to map further data with it, delete it. A deletion does no quantum work, uses no QPU time, and cannot be undone.\n"
msgstr "Pemetaan yang telah dipadankan kekal tersedia sehingga anda memadamnya. Jika anda tidak mahu memetakan data lanjut dengannya, padamkannya. Pemadaman tidak melakukan kerja kuantum, tidak menggunakan masa QPU, dan tidak boleh dibuat asal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr "Kesimpulan {#conclusion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What you accomplished {#what-you-accomplished}"
msgstr "Apa yang telah anda capai {#what-you-accomplished}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, you accomplished the following:\n"
msgstr "Dalam tutorial ini, anda telah mencapai perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepared a real-world credit risk dataset with categorical and numerical attributes for quantum feature extraction.\n"
msgstr "Menyediakan set data risiko kredit dunia sebenar dengan atribut kategori dan berangka untuk pengekstrakan ciri kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Established a classical random forest baseline.\n"
msgstr "Menetapkan garis dasar random forest klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Used Rimay to fit a quantum feature mapping on quantum hardware and map the training and test sets in one run.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan Rimay untuk memadankan pemetaan ciri kuantum pada perkakasan kuantum dan memetakan set latihan dan ujian dalam satu larian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trained the same model on quantum-transformed and on combined features, and compared them with the baseline.\n"
msgstr "Melatih model yang sama pada ciri yang diubah secara kuantum dan pada ciri gabungan, serta membandingkannya dengan garis dasar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key takeaways {#key-takeaways}"
msgstr "Perkara utama {#key-takeaways}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay fits into an existing machine learning pipeline as one additional preprocessing step. You keep your data preparation and your classical model.\n"
msgstr "Rimay sesuai dimuatkan ke dalam saluran paip pembelajaran mesin sedia ada sebagai satu langkah prapemprosesan tambahan. Anda mengekalkan penyediaan data dan model klasik anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of qubits bounds the number of input features, and the number of rows times `shots` bounds the size of a single job.\n"
msgstr "Bilangan qubit menghadkan bilangan ciri input, dan bilangan baris darab `shots` menghadkan saiz sesuatu job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the quantum-transformed features combined with the original features as a default, because the model can use both.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan ciri yang diubah secara kuantum yang digabungkan dengan ciri asal sebagai lalai, kerana model boleh menggunakan kedua-duanya.\n"

